{
  "name": "cloud_deck_survey",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "\u00a725b: WHERE the three decks' sunsets actually sit on the clock, so the A/B scenario beside this one can pick its hours from a measurement rather than from arithmetic.\n\nThis is the survey CLAUDE.md asks for before any scenario picks an hour, and \u00a725b needs it more than most: the whole sequence \u2014 the low deck losing the sun, then the mid deck, then cirrus \u2014 spans elevation 0 to about -4.3 degrees, which at latitude 45 on day 40 is roughly a quarter of an in-game hour end to end. An hourly grid would step straight over it and report the subsystem as absent.\n\nEvery probe is UNPINNED (dummy expectation, huge tolerance): the point is to read numbers out of the report, not to assert them. sun_elevation is sampled beside the two underlit probes at every step, so the hours the A/B then pins are anchored to an elevation as well as to a clock reading.",
